{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Cartel Charter War","logline":"When the Bridge Wardens challenge the Drift Cartel's charter, cartographer Veya and toll-master Kael clash over the last stable skybridge routes, and every isle must choose a side before the network collapses.","theme":"Control costs more than it gains; truth is safer shared than hoarded.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"Cracks in the Charter","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silverspine_charts","title":"The Fading Bridges","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya completes charts showing which skybridges are failing and which routes remain stable. Her wind-sight confirms her late mentor's theory that the isles are drifting apart.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Chart a safe route through the breaking skybridge network.","conflict":"The charts show that the few stable routes are the ones the Cartel's charter claims, and Veya's stubbornness makes her refuse to share the data until she is certain.","outcome":"Veya finishes a draft chart of the last stable routes and decides to take it to the Bridge Wardens at Emberroost."},{"id":"scn_emberroost_warden_claim","title":"Wardens Challenge the Charter","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya shows the Wardens her draft chart. They accuse the Cartel of sabotaging forge-island supplies and resolve to formally challenge the Cartel Charter, which turns the Toll War into open political conflict.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Persuade the Wardens to use her charts to protect the stable routes.","conflict":"The Wardens want to use the charts as a weapon in the charter challenge, while Veya fears becoming an ambitious power-seeker like the cartel leaders.","outcome":"The Wardens file their challenge against the charter using Veya's chart as evidence, and Veya is now publicly tied to the fight.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_charts"]},{"id":"scn_mistral_docks_response","title":"The Toll-Master's Answer","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael learns of the challenge and the existence of Veya's charts. He reads the weakness in the Wardens' position and moves to claim the last stable routes before the bridges collapse.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Seize the last stable skybridge routes and secure the Cartel's monopoly.","conflict":"Kael admires Veya's skill yet knows he cannot let her succeed, and the Wardens publicly accuse him of sabotage, forcing him to act under scrutiny.","outcome":"Kael raises tolls on the stable routes, imposes a grain levy, and orders his enforcers to obtain Veya's charts.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_warden_claim"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Every Isle Must Choose","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_levy","title":"The Levy Reaches The Hollow","summary":"Cartel enforcers arrive at The Hollow to collect the new grain levy. Maris, who knows every secret silo, hides grain and starts planning to smuggle it past the enforcers.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Smuggle enough grain to keep The Hollow fed through the crisis.","conflict":"Enforcers close in on her routes, and her slow trust makes the Hollow Circle reluctant to take outside help.","outcome":"Maris hides the first grain stores and learns the Wardens are looking for allies, which leads her to seek out Veya.","depends_on":["scn_mistral_docks_response"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_alliance","title":"Maps for Paths","summary":"Veya travels to The Hollow, and Maris reluctantly trades her unmapped service corridors for Veya's wind-current knowledge. Together they find a hidden route that bypasses the toll bridges.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Build an alliance that gives both of them a safe route and feeds the isle.","conflict":"Maris distrusts outsiders and Veya refuses to admit her chart has gaps that Maris's paths expose.","outcome":"They agree to trade knowledge, and Veya's chart is improved, but Maris is now tied to the Wardens' fight and exposed to the Cartel.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_levy"]},{"id":"scn_docks_confrontation","title":"Rivals on the Quay","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael confronts Veya, who has come to contest the new tolls. He offers her a place in the Cartel in exchange for her charts, using his charm and Ledger-mastery to find her weakness: her need for recognition.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants the charts, while Veya wants to expose the toll increases and the sabotage.","conflict":"Their shared apprenticeship makes Kael's offer tempting, and Veya cannot admit that the charter protects ships she depends on.","outcome":"Veya refuses but lets slip that her chart is incomplete without the Hollow's paths, which gives Kael the information he needs to pressure Maris.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_alliance"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_raid","title":"Charts Under Siege","summary":"Cartel agents move on Silverspine Academy to bury the charts. Veya races back through Maris's service corridors, arriving in time to save the original charts, but a rival copy is seized.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Protect the charts from the Cartel.","conflict":"Veya's stubbornness delays her warning to the Academy scholars, and Maris risks exposing her secret corridors to save Veya's work.","outcome":"The original charts survive and Maris's corridors are compromised, which leaves her isle vulnerable and strains her trust in Veya.","depends_on":["scn_docks_confrontation"]},{"id":"scn_emberroost_sabotage","title":"The Severed Cable","summary":"Kael pushes the Cartel to seize cable stocks at Emberroost, and a spark in the forge-pit nearly severs a skybridge, which the Wardens blame on Cartel sabotage. Kael sees that his control is the thing endangering the network, but he doubles down.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to cut the Wardens off from supplies, while Veya wants to prove the sabotage and keep the bridge safe.","conflict":"Open flame is forbidden outside shielded forge-pits, so the near-collapse exposes the Cartel's recklessness, but Kael's belief that price equals worth keeps him from backing down.","outcome":"Veya gathers proof of the Cartel's role, Kael's doubts deepen, and the isles are forced to take sides.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_raid"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_betrayal","title":"The Silo Raid","summary":"Using the information Veya let slip, Cartel enforcers raid the secret silos. Maris, who trusts slowly and rarely forgives, confronts Veya, who finally admits her mistake and offers her charts to the Hollow Circle.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants to save the remaining grain, and Veya wants to repair the damage she caused.","conflict":"Maris must choose between loyalty to home and her friendship with Veya, and Veya must overcome her inability to admit fault.","outcome":"Veya admits her mistake and shares the charts openly, and Maris chooses to stand beside her, committing the Hollow Circle to the Wardens' side.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_sabotage"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Charter Tribunal","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_docks_tribunal","title":"Tribunal at Mistral Docks","summary":"The Wardens, the Hollow Circle, and the Cartel gather at Mistral Docks for a public hearing on the charter. Veya presents the shared charts, Maris testifies to the levy and the raids, and Kael argues that regulation alone can prevent collapse.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the charter overturned and the charts made public, while Kael wants to defend the charter and seize the routes.","conflict":"Kael uses Ledger-mastery to attack the Wardens' weakest point, and Veya must admit what she got wrong in front of everyone.","outcome":"Veya's honest admission and the proof from Emberroost sway the isles, and Kael is left with a choice between forcing the charter through and yielding.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_betrayal","scn_emberroost_sabotage"]},{"id":"scn_skybridge_showdown","title":"The Last Stable Bridge","summary":"As the tribunal turns against him, Kael tries to seize the last stable skybridge, which begins to fail under his blockade. Veya's wind-sight and Maris's corridors let them guide the crowds off, and Kael recognises that control is costing the Cartel everything.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to hold the bridge, while Veya and Maris want to get everyone to safety.","conflict":"The bridge is failing, and Kael cannot let Veya succeed but admires her skill, forcing him to choose between his monopoly and the people on the bridge.","outcome":"Kael lifts the blockade, the bridge holds long enough for evacuation, and the Cartel's hold on the routes is broken.","depends_on":["scn_docks_tribunal"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"A Shared Sky","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_charter_rewritten","title":"The Charter Rewritten","summary":"At Silverspine, the Wardens, the Hollow Circle, and a humbled Kael draft a new charter in which the charts are public and tolls fund bridge upkeep. Kael accepts a reduced role, aware of what his control cost.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Establish a fair arrangement for the use of the routes.","conflict":"Old grievances linger, and Maris is slow to forgive Kael while Veya must resist taking the charts' control for herself.","outcome":"The new charter is signed with shared stewardship of the charts, and wind-debt is tied to bridge repair rather than profit.","depends_on":["scn_skybridge_showdown"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"Grain Without Levy","summary":"In The Hollow, the windmills turn again and grain moves freely. Maris recognises that hiding was as brave as standing still, and Veya begins charting the drifting isles with an open door for any who wish to join.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Restore the grain trade and mend the friendship between Maris and Veya.","conflict":"Maris's slow trust and Veya's pride threaten to leave the friendship unresolved.","outcome":"Maris and Veya reaffirm their alliance, the Hollow is fed, and Veya begins sharing her charts widely as the isles continue to drift.","depends_on":["scn_charter_rewritten"]}]}]}
</Output>
