ion_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to cut the Wardens off from supplies, while Veya wants to prove the sabotage and keep the bridge safe.","conflict":"Open flame is forbidden outside shielded forge-pits, so the near-collapse exposes the Cartel's recklessness, but Kael's belief that price equals worth keeps him from backing down.","outcome":"Veya gathers proof of the Cartel's role, Kael's doubts deepen, and the isles are forced to take sides.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_raid"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_betrayal","title":"The Silo Raid","summary":"Using the information Veya let slip, Cartel enforcers raid the secret silos. Maris, who trusts slowly and rarely forgives, confronts Veya, who finally admits her mistake and offers her charts to the Hollow Circle.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants to save the remaining grain, and Veya wants to repair the damage she caused.","conflict":"Maris must choose between loyalty to home and her friendship with Veya, and Veya must overcome her inability to admit fault.","outcome":"Veya admits her mistake and shares the charts openly, and Maris chooses to stand beside her, committing the Hollow Circle to the Wardens' side.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_sabotage"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Charter Tribunal","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_docks_tribunal","title":"Tribunal at Mistral Docks","summary":"The Wardens, the Hollow Circle, and the Cartel gather at Mistral Docks for a public hearing on the charter. Veya presents the shared charts, Maris testifies to the levy and the raids, and Kael argues that regulation alone can prevent collapse.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the charter overturned and the charts made public, while Kael wants to defend the charter and seize the routes.","conflict":"Kael uses Ledger-mastery to attack the Wardens' weakest point, and Veya must admit what she got wrong in front of everyone.","outcome":"Veya's honest admission and the proof from Emberroost sway the isles, and Kael is left with a choice between forcing the charter through and yielding.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_betrayal","scn_emberroost_sabotage"]},{"id":"scn_skybridge_showdown","title":"The Last Stable Bridge","summary":"As the tribunal turns against him, Kael tries to seize the last stable skybridge, which begins to fail under his blockade. Veya's wind-sight and Maris's corridors let them guide the crowds off, and Kael recognises that control is costing the Cartel everything.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to hold the bridge, while Veya and Maris want to get everyone to safety.","conflict":"The bridge is failing, and Kael cannot let Veya succeed but admires her skill, forcing him to choose between his monopoly and the people on the bridge.","outcome":"Kael lifts the blockade, the bridge holds long enough for evacuation, and the Cartel's hold on the routes is broken.","depends_on":["scn_docks_tribunal"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"A Shared Sky","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_charter_rewritten","title":"The Charter Rewritten","summary":"At Silverspine, the Wardens, the Hollow Circle, and a humbled Kael draft a new charter in which the charts are public and tolls fund bridge upkeep. Kael accepts a reduced role, aware of what his control cost.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Establish a fair arrangement for the use of the routes.","conflict":"Old grievances linger, and Maris is slow to forgive Kael while Veya must resist taking the charts' control for herself.","outcome":"The new charter is signed with shared stewardship of the charts, and wind-debt is tied to bridge repair rather than profit.","depends_on":["scn_skybridge_showdown"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"Grain Without Levy","summary":"In The Hollow, the windmills turn again and grain moves freely. Maris recognises that hiding was as brave as standing still, and Veya begins charting the drifting isles with an open door for any who wish to join.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Restore the grain trade and mend the friendship between Maris and Veya.","conflict":"Maris's slow trust and Veya's pride threaten to leave the friendship unresolved.","outcome":"Maris and Veya reaffirm their alliance, the Hollow is fed, and Veya begins sharing her charts widely as the isles continue to drift.","depends_on":["scn_charter_rewritten"]}]}]}
