{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Hollow Calm","logline":"When a windless night strands the isles and something ancient stirs in the abandoned skybridge roots, a stubborn cartographer must share her dangerous charts with her rival before the Drift Cartel's grip on the last stable bridges leaves the archipelago to starve and fall silent.","theme":"Truths shared are safer than truths hoarded.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Wind Dies","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_dead_air_at_silverspine","title":"Dead Air at Silverspine","summary":"On the night the wind stops, Veya's wind-sight goes blank. She sees the colours of the currents drain away and finds her charts of the fading skybridges quivering with a strange, rhythmic pulse that matches no known drift.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Veya wants to confirm whether the calm is natural or the first sign that her late mentor's theory of drifting isles is true.","conflict":"Her wind-sight reads nothing, and her stubbornness makes her dismiss the pulsing pattern as an error in her own charts.","outcome":"Veya recognises the pulse points to the abandoned skybridge roots beneath The Hollow and resolves to chart a route there, telling no one."},{"id":"scn_toll_at_the_docks","title":"Toll at the Docks","summary":"At Mistral Docks, stranded ships crowd the piers. Kael seizes the moment, raising the toll on the few skybridge crossings still holding and demanding wind-debt be repaid immediately in goods.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to lock down the last stable skybridge routes before the calm makes them collapse.","conflict":"Merchants and Bridge Wardens protest that the toll war is strangling the stranded isles, and a Warden accuses him of sabotaging forge-island supplies.","outcome":"Kael forces the new tolls through, but learns that a Silverspine cartographer is charting routes he does not control, so he sends word for her charts to be buried.","depends_on":["scn_dead_air_at_silverspine"]},{"id":"scn_the_levy_and_the_silos","title":"The Levy and the Silos","summary":"In The Hollow, windmills stand motionless and the grain stores run low. Maris learns that Cartel enforcers will collect the grain levy at dawn and begins moving grain through the service corridors she alone knows.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Maris wants to smuggle enough grain into hidden silos to keep The Hollow fed through the crisis.","conflict":"Enforcers are already watching the routes, and her slow trust leaves her working alone and exposed.","outcome":"She hides the first shipment but discovers that one service corridor now ends in a stirred, hollow dark where the old skybridge roots begin and something moves.","depends_on":["scn_toll_at_the_docks"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"What Stirs Below","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_the_crossing_to_the_hollow","title":"The Crossing to The Hollow","summary":"Veya crosses to The Hollow on a skybridge where wind-debt is levied at the gate. With no wind to read, she navigates by the pulse in her charts and meets Maris at the mill, who is hiding grain from the enforcers.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to reach the skybridge roots, and Maris wants to know why a cartographer is trespassing on her isle.","conflict":"Maris distrusts outsiders and Veya refuses to reveal what her charts show, so each withholds what the other needs.","outcome":"They strike a bargain: Veya's chart knowledge for Maris's unmapped corridors, and the two agree to descend together.","depends_on":["scn_dead_air_at_silverspine","scn_the_levy_and_the_silos"]},{"id":"scn_corridors_of_the_roots","title":"Corridors of the Roots","summary":"Maris leads Veya through service corridors into the abandoned skybridge roots, where cloudstone cables hang slack and silent. They find fresh scrapes in the stone and hear a slow breathing in the still air.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to chart the roots and find the source of the pulse.","conflict":"The corridors are unmapped and the windless dark hides the thing that stirs. Veya's wind-sight shows nothing, and her pride keeps her from turning back when Maris urges caution.","outcome":"They find a hollow chamber where the cloudstone has been gnawed through. Veya realises the bridges are failing from below, not from drift, and her mentor's theory is incomplete.","depends_on":["scn_the_crossing_to_the_hollow"]},{"id":"scn_the_toll_masters_offer","title":"The Toll-Master's Offer","summary":"Kael tracks Veya to The Hollow and offers her a seat in the Cartel in exchange for her charts. He charms and pressures her, while his enforcers close in on Maris's smuggling routes.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants Veya's charts handed over so he can seize the last stable routes.","conflict":"Veya is tempted by recognition but fears becoming like him. Maris sees her ally weighing the offer and her trust wavers.","outcome":"Veya refuses to hand over the charts but, unable to admit her theory was wrong, also refuses to tell Kael what she found. Kael leaves with a warning, and Maris decides to hide the grain elsewhere.","depends_on":["scn_corridors_of_the_roots","scn_toll_at_the_docks"]},{"id":"scn_forge_fires_and_sabotage","title":"Forge Fires and Sabotage","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya seeks Bridge Wardens who can reinforce the gnawed roots. She finds the cable-braiding stores short, with Wardens blaming Cartel sabotage, and a fire hazard in the stilled air forces the forge-pits to be shielded.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants cloudstone cable to reinforce the roots, and Kael wants to prove the Wardens' accusations false and keep the supplies under Cartel control.","conflict":"The Wardens will not release scarce cable without proof, and Veya's charts are the only proof. Kael arrives and demands the charts in return for passage, while open flame near the forge-pits endangers the isle.","outcome":"A spark from an unshielded lantern nearly severs a cable. Kael and Veya together smother it, shaking Kael's certainty, but the Wardens still demand Veya share her findings openly.","depends_on":["scn_the_toll_masters_offer"]},{"id":"scn_the_silverspine_council","title":"The Silverspine Council","summary":"Back at the academy, Veya faces the Wardens and scholars. She must admit her mentor's theory is wrong in part, that the isles are not simply drifting but being undermined from below, or lose their support.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the Wardens to commit to a descent into the roots, and Maris wants a guarantee that The Hollow will be protected from the levy.","conflict":"Veya's inability to admit error stalls the council until Maris, torn between home and friendship, speaks for her. The scholars doubt a miller's daughter's testimony.","outcome":"Veya admits her error and shares the full chart. The council agrees to send an expedition, but word reaches Kael, who moves to seize the roots first.","depends_on":["scn_forge_fires_and_sabotage"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Hollow Calm","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_race_to_the_roots","title":"Race to the Roots","summary":"Kael leads Cartel enforcers to the roots to claim the last stable routes, while Veya and Maris take the expedition through Maris's corridors ahead of him. The two groups meet in the dark above the gnawed chamber.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to chart and reinforce a safe route, and Kael wants to seize the roots and the bridges above them.","conflict":"The two sides stand over a chamber where the cloudstone is breaking apart, and neither can claim the route without the other's knowledge: Veya's charts and Kael's ledger-mastery of the Cartel's resources.","outcome":"The thing in the roots stirs and the floor begins to give way, trapping Kael's enforcers and forcing both sides to act together.","depends_on":["scn_the_silverspine_council"]},{"id":"scn_the_breath_beneath","title":"The Breath Beneath","summary":"In the windless dark, the ancient thing slides through the roots and gnaws the last stable cables. Veya uses her charts to guide the group along the weakest points, Maris leads them through the corridors, and Kael spends Cartel cable and goods freely to brace the span.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to save the group and the last bridges, and Kael wants to hold the routes at any cost.","conflict":"Kael's instinct to price every sacrifice nearly costs them the span, and Veya must trust his resources and Maris her rival's word to get everyone out.","outcome":"A faint draught stirs and the creature recoils from the moving air. The group braces the span with Cartel cable and escapes, with the bridge held but badly strained.","depends_on":["scn_race_to_the_roots"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"After the Calm","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_the_wind_returns","title":"The Wind Returns","summary":"As the wind returns across The Hollow, windmills turn again. Kael, shaken, surrenders the cable stores and the levy on the grain to the Wardens and the Hollow Circle, having learned what control cost him.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to atone without losing the Cartel entirely, and Maris wants the levy lifted.","conflict":"Maris does not forgive easily and the Hollow Circle doubts a toll-master's change of heart.","outcome":"Kael lifts the levy and opens the cable stores, and Maris accepts the grain shipments openly, no longer smuggling.","depends_on":["scn_the_breath_beneath"]},{"id":"scn_charts_shared","title":"Charts Shared","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya copies her charts and distributes them to the Wardens, Kael, and the Hollow Circle, replacing her mentor's theory with the truth about the roots and promising a joint watch on the skybridges.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants the charts shared so no one can bury or hoard them.","conflict":"Some scholars resent the revision of her mentor's work, and Kael hesitates to give up the Cartel's advantage in tolls.","outcome":"Kael agrees to a shared toll and watch, ending the toll war for now. Veya accepts that truths shared are safer, and Maris takes a place on the watch.","depends_on":["scn_the_wind_returns"]},{"id":"scn_a_season_of_wind","title":"A Season of Wind","summary":"At Mistral Docks, ships depart on the returning wind and wind-debt is repaid in labour at the bridge repairs. A quiet watch is posted at the roots, and the sound of something distant still lingers in the corridors.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to rebuild trade on fairer terms, and Veya wants to confirm the watch is manned.","conflict":"Cartel merchants resent the lowered tolls, and Veya's charts show the roots still pulse faintly.","outcome":"Kael backs the new terms against his own merchants and Veya leaves to continue charting, aware that the thing below has only withdrawn.","depends_on":["scn_charts_shared"]}]}]}
