,"outcome":"Kael learns that Veya's charts may reveal the stable routes and resolves to obtain them, dispatching enforcers to find her.","depends_on":["scn_veya_charts_breaking"]},{"id":"scn_maris_grain_run","title":"Grain Through the Corridors","summary":"In The Hollow, Maris uses her Pathfinding through unmapped service corridors to move grain past Cartel levy collectors, while the Hollow Circle debates how long it can resist.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Smuggle enough grain to keep The Hollow fed through the crisis and protect her isle from the grain levy.","conflict":"Cartel enforcers are closing in on her routes, and she trusts so slowly that she refuses help even from allies who could ease the burden.","outcome":"Maris completes one run but learns enforcers have found a corridor, and she understands her routes cannot stay hidden alone.","depends_on":["scn_kael_tolls_docks"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Cracks in the Network","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_veya_maris_meet","title":"A Trade of Secrets","summary":"Pursued by enforcers, Veya travels to The Hollow and trades her wind-current knowledge for Maris's secret paths. They form an uneasy alliance.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants Maris's corridor knowledge to verify her chart; Maris wants Veya's wind-reading to keep her routes safe from enforcers.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and Veya will not admit her chart might be incomplete, so each hides part of what she knows.","outcome":"They agree to a limited exchange and together find that one of Veya's charted bridges is wrong, which Veya reluctantly concedes.","depends_on":["scn_veya_charts_breaking","scn_maris_grain_run"]},{"id":"scn_emberroost_sabotage","title":"Cables Cut at Emberroost","summary":"Veya and Maris travel to Emberroost to warn the Bridge Wardens and learn the braided cables are failing from short supplies. Kael's agents are there, and the Wardens blame him for the shortages.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants the Wardens to act on her chart; Kael wants to take the chart and the forge-island's cable stock for the Cartel.","conflict":"Kael is charming but ruthless and Veya refuses to hand over her charts, while the Wardens, suspicious of everyone, cannot tell whom to trust. Veya's pride causes her to withhold the chart's uncertain sections, and the Wardens dismiss it.","outcome":"The Wardens expel Kael's agents but doubt Veya's chart. Kael escapes with a copy of part of it, and Veya realises withholding her uncertainty has cost her credibility.","depends_on":["scn_veya_maris_meet","scn_kael_tolls_docks"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_confrontation","title":"Rivals at Silverspine","summary":"Kael confronts Veya at Silverspine, where they were once apprentices. He offers a Cartel partnership to control the charts and she refuses, though his offer reveals he admires her skill.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants Veya's full charts to claim the last stable routes; Veya wants to stop the Cartel from burying or controlling her work.","conflict":"Kael admires her skill but cannot let her succeed; Veya fears becoming like the ambitious Cartel leaders and cannot admit that his partial copy shows an error in her own work.","outcome":"Veya refuses, but Kael's partial chart exposes a flaw in her route, forcing her to admit she was wrong. Kael leaves with enough to start closing the routes and the Toll War escalates.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_sabotage"]},{"id":"scn_mistral_docks_blockade","title":"The Blockade","summary":"Kael uses the Cartel's lanes to blockade the safest routes and demand grain levies. Maris's smuggling is exposed at Mistral Docks and she is nearly captured, while Veya must choose whether to share her corrected chart.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Maris wants to get her grain through the blockade; Kael wants to enforce the levy and take the routes; Veya wants to reach the docks to warn the merchants.","conflict":"Maris must choose between loyalty to home and her new friendship with Veya when Veya's presence draws enforcers. Kael has the ledger-mastery to find every weak point in their arrangement.","outcome":"Maris escapes by trusting Veya and her wind-sight, and Veya publicly shares her corrected chart with the merchants. Kael's blockade weakens but he still holds the main lanes.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_confrontation","scn_veya_maris_meet"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Drift Breaks","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_gathering","title":"Gathering the Circle","summary":"In The Hollow, Maris persuades the Hollow Circle to share its hidden corridors with the Wardens and merchants, and Veya shares the full chart. The three plan a coordinated crossing before the last bridges fail.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Unite the Hollow Circle, the Wardens and the merchants behind one route plan to cross before the bridges collapse.","conflict":"Maris must overcome her mistrust and Veya must accept correction from others, while the Circle fears the Cartel's reprisals.","outcome":"The plan is agreed, with Maris providing the corridors and Veya the chart, though they know Kael's blockade still stands between them and safety.","depends_on":["scn_mistral_docks_blockade"]},{"id":"scn_emberroost_final_crossing","title":"The Last Crossing","summary":"As the skybridge cables fail at Emberroost, Veya and Maris lead the crossing while Kael arrives to seize the last stable route. When the bridge begins to give way, Kael must choose between control and cooperation.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want to lead the isles across the last stable route; Kael wants to seize and close it for the Cartel.","conflict":"The bridge is failing and Kael's seizure would strand everyone, but without his ledger-mastery to untangle the Cartel's blockade they cannot all cross in time.","outcome":"Kael realises control costs more than it gains and uses his ledger-mastery to release the blockade. Veya's chart and Maris's corridors let the crossing succeed, and the bridge holds long enough for all to cross.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_gathering"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"New Currents","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silverspine_new_charts","title":"Charts Shared","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya publishes her charts openly and credits Maris and Kael, accepting the corrections that improved them. The Wardens begin rebuilding with shared knowledge.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to share the charts so the isles can use them and prove her mentor's theory honestly.","conflict":"Some scholars resist an open chart that admits error, and Veya must resist the urge to claim sole credit.","outcome":"Veya learns that truths shared are safer than truths hoarded; the charts are published and the Wardens begin repairing the safest routes.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_final_crossing"]},{"id":"scn_mistral_docks_accounting","title":"The Cartel's Reckoning","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael faces the Cartel and the Wardens, renouncing the levy and tolls that fuelled the Toll War. He settles his own wind-debt in labour repairing bridges.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to repair what his control cost and settle his wind-debt rather than abandon the trade he believes in.","conflict":"The Cartel princes accuse him of weakness, and he must stop equating price with worth to defend his choice.","outcome":"Kael lifts the grain levy and agrees to fair tolls, and his rivalry with Veya turns into wary respect. The Toll War eases.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_new_charts"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"A Fed Archipelago","summary":"Back in The Hollow, Maris watches the windmills turn and grain flow openly across the repaired bridges. She understands that hiding was brave, but standing together is braver still.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Maris wants to see The Hollow fed openly and to settle her trust in the people who helped.","conflict":"Maris must decide whether to forgive Kael, whose levy once threatened her home.","outcome":"Maris accepts Kael's repayment, keeps her friendship with Veya and stops hiding, and the three share a harvest that marks the beginning of a more cooperative archipelago.","depends_on":["scn_mistral_docks_accounting"]}]}]}
