cter_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Maris wants to get her grain through the blockade; Kael wants to enforce the levy and take the routes; Veya wants to reach the docks to warn the merchants.","conflict":"Maris must choose between loyalty to home and her new friendship with Veya when Veya's presence draws enforcers. Kael has the ledger-mastery to find every weak point in their arrangement.","outcome":"Maris escapes by trusting Veya and her wind-sight, and Veya publicly shares her corrected chart with the merchants. Kael's blockade weakens but he still holds the main lanes.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_confrontation","scn_veya_maris_meet"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Drift Breaks","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_gathering","title":"Gathering the Circle","summary":"In The Hollow, Maris persuades the Hollow Circle to share its hidden corridors with the Wardens and merchants, and Veya shares the full chart. The three plan a coordinated crossing before the last bridges fail.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Unite the Hollow Circle, the Wardens and the merchants behind one route plan to cross before the bridges collapse.","conflict":"Maris must overcome her mistrust and Veya must accept correction from others, while the Circle fears the Cartel's reprisals.","outcome":"The plan is agreed, with Maris providing the corridors and Veya the chart, though they know Kael's blockade still stands between them and safety.","depends_on":["scn_mistral_docks_blockade"]},{"id":"scn_emberroost_final_crossing","title":"The Last Crossing","summary":"As the skybridge cables fail at Emberroost, Veya and Maris lead the crossing while Kael arrives to seize the last stable route. When the bridge begins to give way, Kael must choose between control and cooperation.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want to lead the isles across the last stable route; Kael wants to seize and close it for the Cartel.","conflict":"The bridge is failing and Kael's seizure would strand everyone, but without his ledger-mastery to untangle the Cartel's blockade they cannot all cross in time.","outcome":"Kael realises control costs more than it gains and uses his ledger-mastery to release the blockade. Veya's chart and Maris's corridors let the crossing succeed, and the bridge holds long enough for all to cross.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_gathering"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"New Currents","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silverspine_new_charts","title":"Charts Shared","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya publishes her charts openly and credits Maris and Kael, accepting the corrections that improved them. The Wardens begin rebuilding with shared knowledge.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to share the charts so the isles can use them and prove her mentor's theory honestly.","conflict":"Some scholars resist an open chart that admits error, and Veya must resist the urge to claim sole credit.","outcome":"Veya learns that truths shared are safer than truths hoarded; the charts are published and the Wardens begin repairing the safest routes.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_final_crossing"]},{"id":"scn_mistral_docks_accounting","title":"The Cartel's Reckoning","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael faces the Cartel and the Wardens, renouncing the levy and tolls that fuelled the Toll War. He settles his own wind-debt in labour repairing bridges.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to repair what his control cost and settle his wind-debt rather than abandon the trade he believes in.","conflict":"The Cartel princes accuse him of weakness, and he must stop equating price with worth to defend his choice.","outcome":"Kael lifts the grain levy and agrees to fair tolls, and his rivalry with Veya turns into wary respect. The Toll War eases.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_new_charts"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"A Fed Archipelago","summary":"Back in The Hollow, Maris watches the windmills turn and grain flow openly across the repaired bridges. She understands that hiding was brave, but standing together is braver still.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Maris wants to see The Hollow fed openly and to settle her trust in the people who helped.","conflict":"Maris must decide whether to forgive Kael, whose levy once threatened her home.","outcome":"Maris accepts Kael's repayment, keeps her friendship with Veya and stops hiding, and the three share a harvest that marks the beginning of a more cooperative archipelago.","depends_on":["scn_mistral_docks_accounting"]}]}]}
