ights to her charts. She remembers they were apprentices together and refuses.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants the charts. Veya wants to keep them out of Cartel hands.","conflict":"Veya wants recognition but fears becoming like the Cartel leaders. Kael's offer is tempting, and she is too stubborn to say so.","outcome":"Veya refuses and Kael leaves with a veiled warning. She decides to protect her charts by leaving for the lower isles.","depends_on":["scn_kael_at_the_docks"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Closing Currents","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_the_hollows_secret_paths","title":"The Hollow's Secret Paths","summary":"Veya reaches The Hollow and meets Maris, who is smuggling grain to dodge the Cartel levy. They agree to trade wind-current knowledge for Maris's unmapped service corridors.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to find a hidden route that avoids Cartel watchers. Maris wants to keep The Hollow fed.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and suspects Veya will draw the Cartel to her silos. Veya is reluctant to share her unfinished work.","outcome":"They form a cautious alliance and Maris shows Veya the corridors between the windmills and granaries.","depends_on":["scn_the_request_refused"]},{"id":"scn_the_levy_enforcers","title":"The Levy Enforcers","summary":"Cartel enforcers close in on Maris's smuggling routes at The Hollow. Veya's wind-sight and Maris's corridors let them slip away with only part of the grain.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Get the grain shipment out past the enforcers.","conflict":"The enforcers follow the trail that Veya's open use of her charts left behind. Maris must choose between loyalty to home and her new friendship.","outcome":"The grain gets through and The Hollow is safe for now, but Maris learns that Veya's carelessness exposed her routes.","depends_on":["scn_the_hollows_secret_paths"]},{"id":"scn_forge_island_sabotage","title":"Cables at Emberroost","summary":"Veya and Maris travel to Emberroost to warn the Bridge Wardens that a key cloudstone cable is failing. Kael arrives, and each side blames the other for the damaged supplies.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants the Wardens to act on her charts. Kael wants control of the surviving routes.","conflict":"Veya refuses to admit her charts are incomplete when the Wardens ask about the new pressure front. Kael uses her silence to suggest the Wardens are unreliable.","outcome":"The Wardens delay action, and Kael leaves with a promise to expose Veya as a fraud if the cable fails.","depends_on":["scn_the_levy_enforcers"]},{"id":"scn_the_unreadable_front","title":"The Unreadable Front","summary":"A new storm forms over the archipelago. Veya tries to read it and her wind-sight fails. She finally admits to Maris that her gift has limits.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Predict the storm's path and warn the isles before it hits.","conflict":"The storm moves unlike any current she knows. Her flaw has already cost her the time she needed.","outcome":"Veya admits her limit and Maris proposes pooling everyone's knowledge, including the Cartel's shipping records and the Wardens' cable surveys.","depends_on":["scn_forge_island_sabotage"]},{"id":"scn_kaels_gambit","title":"Kael's Gambit","summary":"As the storm closes in, Kael moves to close the toll gates at Mistral Docks and claim the last stable bridges for the Cartel. Veya confronts him with the truth about the storm.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to lock down the stable routes. Veya wants him to open the lanes for a shared plan.","conflict":"Kael believes control is the only protection and equates price with worth. Veya must trust a rival with her incomplete charts.","outcome":"Kael refuses publicly but privately keeps the charts she left behind. Veya and Maris leave to rally the other isles.","depends_on":["scn_the_unreadable_front"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Storm Crossing","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_the_gathering_at_silverspine","title":"The Gathering at Silverspine","summary":"Veya shares her charts openly with the Wardens, the Hollow Circle and Academy cartographers. Together they build a plan that uses Maris's corridors and the Wardens' cable surveys instead of prediction.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Build a route-by-route survival plan that does not rely on wind-sight alone.","conflict":"Years of distrust divide the factions, and Veya must set aside her wish to be the one who is right.","outcome":"The factions agree to stagger crossings, shore up the weakest bridges and shelter grain and people in the sturdiest isles.","depends_on":["scn_kaels_gambit"]},{"id":"scn_the_storm_breaks","title":"The Storm Breaks","summary":"The storm hits as the plan begins. Veya relays her partial readings, Maris leads people through the service corridors, and Kael arrives at Emberroost to seize the stable bridges.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to hold the cable and get crossings finished. Kael wants to claim the last bridges for the Cartel.","conflict":"Kael's toll gates block the evacuation. Veya's wind-sight cannot say which cable will fail first.","outcome":"A cable begins to fail. Kael sees that locking the gates will strand the Cartel's own ships and families too.","depends_on":["scn_the_gathering_at_silverspine"]},{"id":"scn_the_gates_open","title":"The Gates Open","summary":"Kael must choose between his monopoly and the survival of the isles. Veya offers him the charts openly and asks him to use his ledger-mastery to find where the plan is weakest.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Persuade Kael to open the gates and share control of the routes.","conflict":"Kael's belief that control is the only safeguard clashes with Veya's need to trust him with her work.","outcome":"Kael opens the toll gates and reallocates the Cartel's ships and crossings. The plan holds, and the isles survive the storm.","depends_on":["scn_the_storm_breaks"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"Shared Charts","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_counting_the_cost","title":"Counting the Cost","summary":"At Mistral Docks, the isles tally the damage. Kael faces the Cartel's anger over the lost tolls, and the Wardens and Hollow Circle press him on the levies and tolls.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Settle the toll and levy disputes that the storm made visible.","conflict":"Kael has to accept that control cost him more than it gained. The Cartel's princes still want their monopoly.","outcome":"Kael agrees to lower the tolls and suspend the grain levy in exchange for shared survey work, which is a fragile truce.","depends_on":["scn_the_gates_open"]},{"id":"scn_the_open_atlas","title":"The Open Atlas","summary":"Veya returns to Silverspine and publishes her charts openly, with her wind-sight's limits written beside every reading. The Academy starts an atlas that combines wind-sight, cable surveys and Maris's corridors.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Turn the survival plan into a lasting shared atlas.","conflict":"Veya still struggles to admit mistakes in public, and some scholars doubt a cartographer who has admitted her gift failed.","outcome":"The atlas is accepted, and Veya's mentor's theory is tested by many hands rather than proved by one.","depends_on":["scn_counting_the_cost"]},{"id":"scn_the_hollow_endures","title":"The Hollow Endures","summary":"Maris returns to The Hollow, where 