ve way.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Protect the stored grain and get the villagers clear.","conflict":"Veya's stubborn insistence on her own reading of a bridge leads to a collapse that costs part of the harvest, and Maris must decide whether to forgive her.","outcome":"Most of the grain is saved but part is lost, and Maris's trust in Veya is damaged though not broken.","depends_on":["scn_kael_hunts_charts"]}},{"id":"scn_silverspine_council","title":"The Academy Refuses","summary":"Veya returns to Silverspine with her completed charts. The Academy council, pressured by Cartel influence, refuses to publish them. She is tempted to guard the charts herself instead of sharing them.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Have the Academy publish the charts so every isle can use them.","conflict":"Cartel pressure silences the council, and Veya's fear of becoming like the cartel leaders clashes with her wish for recognition.","outcome":"Veya takes the charts away unpublished, and Maris warns her that hoarding them will cost the isles.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_raid"]}},{"id":"scn_kael_veya_bargain","title":"The Offer at the Bridge","summary":"Kael meets Veya at a failing skybridge and offers a deal: she gives him the charts and he keeps the Cartel's toll lanes open to the Hollow. He reveals he knows the bridges will soon collapse.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants Veya's charts. Veya wants to stop the Toll War without surrendering them.","conflict":"Veya cannot admit her charts could be used for anything but control, and Kael equates price with worth, so he cannot see why she refuses.","outcome":"Veya refuses, and the bridge begins to fail, which forces both to flee and sets the final confrontation.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_council"]}}]},{"id":"act_climax_crossing","title":"The Great Crossing","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_climax_mistral_gathering","title":"The Gathering at Mistral Docks","summary":"Veya brings her charts to the crowded Docks and chooses to share them openly. Kael and the Cartel try to seize them, and Maris leads the Hollow Circle's smugglers through the docks to guard the crowd.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the charts shared with all the isles. Kael wants to seize the last stable routes and the charts.","conflict":"Kael's Cartel enforcers confront Veya and Maris, and Veya must admit her earlier mistakes to win the crowd's trust.","outcome":"Veya admits she was wrong about the bridge, the crowd takes the charts, and Kael's hold on the routes begins to break.","depends_on":["scn_kael_veya_bargain"]}},{"id":"scn_climax_final_bridge","title":"The Last Stable Bridge","summary":"A major skybridge begins to fail with Kael on it. Veya reads the wind currents and guides him across a safe route, while Maris uses her pathfinding to lead others to safety.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Get everyone off the failing bridge before it falls.","conflict":"Kael first refuses her help because he believes control is worth more than trust, and the wind shifts faster than Veya expected.","outcome":"Kael accepts Veya's guidance and survives, and he discovers that control costs more than it gains.","depends_on":["scn_climax_mistral_gathering"]}}]},{"id":"act_resolution_aftermath","title":"The Shared Map","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_resolution_toll_ends","title":"The Tolls Lifted","summary":"Kael gives up his hold on the toll lanes and ends the grain levy, as the shared charts show that hoarding the routes would only lead to collapse. The Wardens and Cartel agree to repay wind-debts in shared labour.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"End the Toll War and the Grain Levy.","conflict":"Cartel factions resist losing their monopoly, and Kael must act against his own long-held belief that price equals worth.","outcome":"The tolls are lifted and the levy ends, and the Cartel's grip loosens.","depends_on":["scn_climax_final_bridge"]}},{"id":"scn_resolution_hollow_feast","title":"Bread for the Archipelago","summary":"Maris returns to The Hollow and opens the silos for everyone. She accepts that hiding can be as brave as standing still and forgives Veya, who delivers the final charts to the Hollow Circle.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Feed the archipelago openly and repair the friendship between Maris and Veya.","conflict":"Maris still struggles to forgive, and some villagers distrust sharing their secret corridors.","outcome":"Maris forgives Veya and the corridors are opened to all, which secures the Hollow's place in the new order.","depends_on":["scn_resolution_toll_ends"]}},{"id":"scn_resolution_academy_publishes","title":"The Charts Published","summary":"Veya returns to Silverspine and has the charts published, giving credit to her late mentor and to Maris. She learns that some truths are safer shared than hoarded.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Publish the charts so the archipelago can navigate the drifting bridges.","conflict":"Veya's pride makes her reluctant to share credit, and Kael's arrival tests whether she can accept him as a former rival.","outcome":"The charts are published and Veya's mentor is vindicated, and the isles begin planning for a drifting archipelago together.","depends_on":["scn_resolution_hollow_feast"]}}]}]}
