{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Archipelago Chronicle","logline":"As the skybridges that bind Aetheria begin to fail, a stubborn cartographer races to chart a safe route while a charming Drift Cartel toll-master tries to seize the last stable bridges, and both must decide whether truth and control are worth what they cost.","theme":"Shared truth outlasts hoarded control","acts":[{"id":"act_setup_charts","title":"The Fading Bridges","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_veya_maps_fading_bridge","title":"The Colour of Failing Wind","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya reads the wind currents with her wind-sight and finds that a major skybridge is drifting out of true, matching her late mentor's theory that the isles are drifting apart.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Confirm that the bridge's movement matches her mentor's theory of drifting isles.","conflict":"The Academy's senior cartographers dismiss the theory, and Veya's stubbornness makes her refuse to hear their doubts about her readings.","outcome":"Veya decides to chart the whole breaking network, and she keeps the early findings to herself rather than share them."}},{"id":"scn_kael_raises_tolls","title":"The Ledger at Mistral Docks","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael uses his ledger-mastery to find the weak points in the shipping contracts. He raises skybridge tolls and plans to secure the last stable routes for the Cartel before the bridges collapse.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Lock merchants into new toll agreements that favour the Drift Cartel's monopoly.","conflict":"Merchants resist the rising tolls, and the Bridge Wardens accuse Kael of sabotaging forge-island supplies.","outcome":"Kael forces the agreements through and begins asking which bridges will outlast the rest, which creates his need for Veya's charts.","depends_on":[]}},{"id":"scn_veya_kael_dockside","title":"Old Apprentices","summary":"Veya travels to Mistral Docks to buy passage to Emberroost. She meets Kael, her former fellow apprentice, who admires her skill and offers her a Cartel-funded survey in exchange for exclusive rights to her charts.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants passage to Emberroost without owing the Cartel. Kael wants to secure her charts.","conflict":"Veya fears becoming like the ambitious cartel leaders and refuses, while Kael admires her yet cannot let her succeed independently.","outcome":"Veya refuses the offer and leaves, and Kael quietly marks her as a threat to the Cartel.","depends_on":["scn_veya_maps_fading_bridge","scn_kael_raises_tolls"]}]},{"id":"act_rising_threads","title":"Threads Under Strain","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_cables","title":"Cables Left Unbraided","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya finds the forge-island short of cloudstone and the Wardens struggling to braid replacement cables. She sees that the shortage matches the Cartel's sabotage claims and that her charts show bridges failing sooner than expected.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Learn which bridges the Wardens can still repair and gather evidence of the supply shortage.","conflict":"Wardens are suspicious of an Academy outsider, and Veya's refusal to admit a mistaken reading about one bridge nearly leads to a deadly crossing.","outcome":"Veya earns the Wardens' grudging trust, and the Wardens give her access to their repair logs.","depends_on":["scn_veya_kael_dockside"]}},{"id":"scn_maris_smuggling","title":"Silos in the Dark","summary":"On The Hollow, Maris moves grain through unmapped service corridors to dodge the Cartel's levy. Cartel enforcers have found one of her routes, which forces her to hide the grain and abandon a corridor.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Smuggle enough grain to keep The Hollow fed through the crisis.","conflict":"Cartel enforcers close in on her routes, and her slow trust of outsiders makes her refuse help from anyone she does not know.","outcome":"Maris saves most of the grain but loses a corridor, and she realises she needs a source of knowledge about the shifting bridges.","depends_on":["scn_kael_raises_tolls"]}},{"id":"scn_veya_meets_maris","title":"Trading Winds for Paths","summary":"Veya travels to The Hollow to study the old windmill routes. Maris catches her in a granary corridor, and after a tense standoff the two agree to trade wind-current knowledge for Maris's secret paths.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the unmapped corridors for her charts. Maris wants a way to predict which bridges will hold.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and suspects Veya is a Cartel spy, while Veya refuses to admit her charts have gaps.","outcome":"They form an alliance, and Veya learns of the unmapped corridors that Maris uses to move grain.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_cables","scn_maris_smuggling"]}},{"id":"scn_kael_hunts_charts","title":"The Toll-Master's Pressure","summary":"Kael learns that Veya is allied with the Hollow and the Wardens. He has enforcers tighten the grain levy and delays Warden shipments to cut her off, while he privately struggles with his respect for her skill.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Cut Veya off from supplies and allies so her charts cannot spread.","conflict":"His admiration for Veya makes him hesitate, and the delays bring open accusations from the Wardens that fuel the Toll War.","outcome":"The levy tightens and the Toll War escalates, and Kael sends enforcers to The Hollow.","depends_on":["scn_veya_meets_maris"]}},{"id":"scn_hollow_raid","title":"The Raid on the Granaries","summary":"Cartel enforcers raid The Hollow. Maris leads them through the service corridors to save the grain stores, while Veya uses her wind-sight to warn which corridor bridges will give way.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Protect the stored grain and get the villagers clear.","conflict":"Veya's stubborn insistence on her own reading of a bridge leads to a collapse that costs part of the harvest, and Maris must decide whether to forgive her.","outcome":"Most of the grain is saved but part is lost, and Maris's trust in Veya is damaged though not broken.","depends_on":["scn_kael_hunts_charts"]}},{"id":"scn_silverspine_council","title":"The Academy Refuses","summary":"Veya returns to Silverspine with her completed charts. The Academy council, pressured by Cartel influence, refuses to publish them. She is tempted to guard the charts herself instead of sharing them.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Have the Academy publish the charts so every isle can use them.","conflict":"Cartel pressure silences the council, and Veya's fear of becoming like the cartel leaders clashes with her wish for recognition.","outcome":"Veya takes the charts away unpublished, and Maris warns her that hoarding them will cost the isles.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_raid"]}},{"id":"scn_kael_veya_bargain","title":"The Offer at the Bridge","summary":"Kael meets Veya at a failing skybridge and offers a deal: she gives him the charts and he keeps the Cartel's toll lanes open to the Hollow. He reveals he knows the bridges will soon collapse.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants Veya's charts. Veya wants to stop the Toll War without surrendering them.","conflict":"Veya cannot admit her charts could be used for anything but control, and Kael equates price with worth, so he cannot see why she refuses.","outcome":"Veya refuses, and the bridge begins to fail, which forces both to flee and sets the final confrontation.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_council"]}}]},{"id":"act_climax_crossing","title":"The Great Crossing","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_climax_mistral_gathering","title":"The Gathering at Mistral Docks","summary":"Veya brings her charts to the crowded Docks and chooses to share them openly. Kael and the Cartel try to seize them, and Maris leads the Hollow Circle's smugglers through the docks to guard the crowd.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the charts shared with all the isles. Kael wants to seize the last stable routes and the charts.","conflict":"Kael's Cartel enforcers confront Veya and Maris, and Veya must admit her earlier mistakes to win the crowd's trust.","outcome":"Veya admits she was wrong about the bridge, the crowd takes the charts, and Kael's hold on the routes begins to break.","depends_on":["scn_kael_veya_bargain"]}},{"id":"scn_climax_final_bridge","title":"The Last Stable Bridge","summary":"A major skybridge begins to fail with Kael on it. Veya reads the wind currents and guides him across a safe route, while Maris uses her pathfinding to lead others to safety.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Get everyone off the failing bridge before it falls.","conflict":"Kael first refuses her help because he believes control is worth more than trust, and the wind shifts faster than Veya expected.","outcome":"Kael accepts Veya's guidance and survives, and he discovers that control costs more than it gains.","depends_on":["scn_climax_mistral_gathering"]}}]},{"id":"act_resolution_aftermath","title":"The Shared Map","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_resolution_toll_ends","title":"The Tolls Lifted","summary":"Kael gives up his hold on the toll lanes and ends the grain levy, as the shared charts show that hoarding the routes would only lead to collapse. The Wardens and Cartel agree to repay wind-debts in shared labour.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"End the Toll War and the Grain Levy.","conflict":"Cartel factions resist losing their monopoly, and Kael must act against his own long-held belief that price equals worth.","outcome":"The tolls are lifted and the levy ends, and the Cartel's grip loosens.","depends_on":["scn_climax_final_bridge"]}},{"id":"scn_resolution_hollow_feast","title":"Bread for the Archipelago","summary":"Maris returns to The Hollow and opens the silos for everyone. She accepts that hiding can be as brave as standing still and forgives Veya, who delivers the final charts to the Hollow Circle.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Feed the archipelago openly and repair the friendship between Maris and Veya.","conflict":"Maris still struggles to forgive, and some villagers distrust sharing their secret corridors.","outcome":"Maris forgives Veya and the corridors are opened to all, which secures the Hollow's place in the new order.","depends_on":["scn_resolution_toll_ends"]}},{"id":"scn_resolution_academy_publishes","title":"The Charts Published","summary":"Veya returns to Silverspine and has the charts published, giving credit to her late mentor and to Maris. She learns that some truths are safer shared than hoarded.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Publish the charts so the archipelago can navigate the drifting bridges.","conflict":"Veya's pride makes her reluctant to share credit, and Kael's arrival tests whether she can accept him as a former rival.","outcome":"The charts are published and Veya's mentor is vindicated, and the isles begin planning for a drifting archipelago together.","depends_on":["scn_resolution_hollow_feast"]}}]}]}
