way to keep the isles trading.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to buy or coerce the map from Veya; Veya wants to learn how much the Cartel knows.","conflict":"Veya is tempted by recognition and resources but fears becoming like the ambitious Cartel leaders, while Kael equates price with worth and cannot understand her refusal.","outcome":"Veya refuses, stubbornly insisting the map is safe, and Kael quietly tells his enforcers to follow her back toward Silverspine.","depends_on":["scn_secret_corridors"]},{"id":"scn_the_false_margin","title":"The False Margin","summary":"Back at Silverspine, Veya compares the map against Maris's corridors and finds the hostile command is tied to a false route that would send travellers across a failing bridge. Her wind-sight shows the trap is real, and she must admit her earlier certainty was wrong.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Separate the true routes from the poisoned ones in the map.","conflict":"Veya cannot admit she was wrong to trust the map, and Maris, who rarely forgives, nearly walks away when she learns Veya hid the command from her.","outcome":"Veya apologises, Maris stays, and together they mark a safe route that exists only in their combined knowledge, which makes both of them targets.","depends_on":["scn_the_toll_masters_offer"]},{"id":"scn_enforcers_at_the_granary","title":"Enforcers at the Granary","summary":"Cartel enforcers raid The Hollow's silos and Maris's smuggling routes to flush out the map. Maris uses her pathfinding to lead them away, but a grain shipment is seized and the Hollow Circle suffers.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Protect the Hollow's grain and the map from the enforcers.","conflict":"Maris must choose between loyalty to home and her friendship with Veya, and Veya's stubborn insistence on carrying the map along puts the isle at risk.","outcome":"They escape with the map but lose part of the harvest; Veya recognises that hoarding the route endangers everyone and decides to share it with the Wardens.","depends_on":["scn_the_false_margin"]},{"id":"scn_the_wardens_gamble","title":"The Wardens' Gamble","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya presents the corrected route to the Bridge Wardens and learns that Kael means to claim the last stable bridge. The Wardens agree to reinforce the route, but they need time and a distraction.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Win the Wardens' support and secure the safe route before the Cartel takes it.","conflict":"Kael arrives with a toll writ claiming the route under the Cartel's charter, and the Wardens fear a break in the Toll War.","outcome":"The Wardens stall Kael with a formal dispute, and Veya, Maris and the Wardens set out to cross the route before he can close it.","depends_on":["scn_enforcers_at_the_granary"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Last Bridge","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_crossing_the_last_bridge","title":"Crossing the Last Bridge","summary":"Veya leads a party across the corrected route while Kael's enforcers press from behind. Her wind-sight reads the bridge's failing currents, and the map's false margin tries once more to command her to take the poisoned path.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Reach the stable route and prove the corrected map saves lives; Kael wants to take the route and the map.","conflict":"The map's hostile command pulls at Veya's pride, Kael pushes her to trade the map for safe passage, and Maris must trust Veya despite her doubts.","outcome":"Veya resists the command, shares the true route openly with everyone present, and Kael's seized copy of the poisoned path begins to fail beneath his enforcers.","depends_on":["scn_the_wardens_gamble"]},{"id":"scn_the_cost_of_control","title":"The Cost of Control","summary":"As the bridge under the Cartel's enforcers frays, Kael has the chance to cut them loose and keep the route for himself. He sees that his hold on the route would cost lives and lets Veya's shared chart guide his people to safety.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to save his enforcers and keep the route; Veya wants to bring everyone across.","conflict":"Kael's belief that price equals worth clashes with Veya's openness, and his admiration for her skill collides with his need to win.","outcome":"Kael yields the route, helping Veya guide the crossing, and the Cartel's monopoly on the last stable bridge is broken.","depends_on":["scn_crossing_the_last_bridge"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"Charts Shared","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_burning_the_margin","title":"Burning the Margin","summary":"At Emberroost, in a shielded forge-pit that keeps open flame from the skybridges, Veya and the Wardens destroy the poisoned margin of the map. They preserve the verified routes as shared charts.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Neutralise the hostile command and make the verified routes public.","conflict":"Veya is tempted to keep the original map as proof of her mentor's theory, but the command still pulls at anyone who reads it.","outcome":"The poisoned margin is burned safely, the true routes are copied for all isles, and Veya accepts that shared truth outweighs personal recognition.","depends_on":["scn_the_cost_of_control"]},{"id":"scn_a_season_of_wind_debt","title":"A Season of Wind-Debt","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael negotiates a new toll arrangement with the Wardens and lifts the grain levy on The Hollow. Maris returns home with her harvest, and Veya begins charting the next season of drift.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Settle the immediate consequences of the crisis and restore trade on the shared routes.","conflict":"Kael's Cartel allies resent the lost monopoly, and old wounds between Maris and the Cartel remain unhealed.","outcome":"A fragile peace takes hold: wind-debts are eased, the Hollow is fed, and Veya's shared charts keep the isles connected, though the eerie map's origin remains unexplained.","depends_on":["scn_burning_the_margin"]}]}]}
