tral bridge and decides her charts must be secured or buried.","depends_on":["scn_veya_charts_drift"]},{"id":"scn_maris_hidden_grain","title":"Silos Beneath the Windmills","summary":"In The Hollow, Maris moves grain through her unmapped service corridors to hide it from the Cartel's levy. She learns that Cartel enforcers are asking about her routes. She also learns that Veya has been seeking paths to Emberroost.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Smuggle enough grain to keep The Hollow fed through the crisis.","conflict":"Cartel enforcers are closing in. Maris does not trust Veya, and Veya arrives needing the corridors.","outcome":"Maris reluctantly trades her secret paths for Veya's wind-current knowledge. The two form an uneasy alliance.","depends_on":["scn_veya_charts_drift","scn_kael_tightens_tolls"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Two Truths at Once","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_cables","title":"Braided Contradiction","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya and Maris examine the cables of the central skybridge. The cloudstone is fraying, yet the surviving braids are somehow bearing more load than the bridge should be able to carry. Veya concludes the bridge is held together by the crossings and the wind-debt the people owe it.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Find the cause of the central skybridge's contradictory behaviour.","conflict":"Veya will not admit that her mentor's theory may be incomplete. Forge-pit rules forbid open flame, and the Wardens distrust outsiders.","outcome":"Veya finds that the bridge's strength depends on shared crossings, but she keeps the finding secret instead of reporting it.","depends_on":["scn_maris_hidden_grain"]},{"id":"scn_kael_confronts_veya","title":"A Rival's Offer","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael confronts Veya, his old fellow apprentice. He offers her fame and protection if she hands over her charts. She refuses, but his charm unsettles her because it echoes her own hunger for recognition.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to secure Veya's charts. Veya wants to keep them out of Cartel hands.","conflict":"Kael admires Veya yet cannot let her succeed. Veya fears becoming like the cartel leaders, while Maris is exposed to the enforcers.","outcome":"Veya escapes with her charts, but Kael now knows the bridge's secret is tied to crossings. Maris's smuggling route is compromised.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_cables"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_dispute","title":"The Academy Refuses","summary":"Veya returns to Silverspine and presents her theory. The Academy and the Bridge Wardens dismiss it, because she has hoarded her data until it looks incomplete. Veya's refusal to admit a flaw in her model costs her allies when she most needs them.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Win the Wardens' backing to keep the central skybridge open.","conflict":"Her stubbornness and her secrecy undermine her credibility, and the Wardens think she is serving the Cartel.","outcome":"Veya is discredited and left isolated. She realises she must share the truth openly rather than hoard it.","depends_on":["scn_kael_confronts_veya"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_betrayal_choice","title":"Home or Friend","summary":"In The Hollow, Cartel enforcers corner Maris. Kael offers to spare the isle's grain if she gives up Veya's location. Maris, who trusts slowly and rarely forgives, must choose between her isle and her friend.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Maris wants to protect The Hollow. Kael wants Veya's whereabouts and charts.","conflict":"Maris's loyalty to home pulls against her bond with Veya, and Kael's leverage over the grain is real.","outcome":"Maris stalls him with a false trail through her hidden corridors and chooses to hide rather than betray. She warns Veya that Kael is moving on the central bridge.","depends_on":["scn_kael_confronts_veya","scn_silverspine_dispute"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Central Skybridge","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_bridge_standoff","title":"The Bridge That Is and Is Not","summary":"On the central skybridge, Kael arrives to claim it with Cartel enforcers. Veya reads its colours and sees that it is collapsing under the Cartel's control and holding under shared passage. She tells Kael and the gathered travellers the whole truth, and the bridge reacts as the crowd crosses.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to get the travellers across safely and share her charts. Kael wants to seize the last stable route.","conflict":"Kael's ledger-mastery shows him that seizing the bridge will break it, but giving up control contradicts everything he believes. Veya must admit she was wrong to hoard her findings.","outcome":"Veya publicly admits her mistake and hands out the charts. Maris leads the travellers along her service corridors onto the bridge, while Kael's claimed span collapses behind his toll gate.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_betrayal_choice"]},{"id":"scn_bridge_choice","title":"What Control Costs","summary":"With the Cartel's span falling and the shared span standing, Kael faces the contradiction directly. He can keep grasping the tolls and fall with them, or let the bridge belong to everyone who crosses. He releases the toll gate, and the bridge settles into the dual state: it collapses for control and stands for trust.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to keep control of the route. Veya wants to save him and the bridge.","conflict":"Kael's flaw, equating price with worth, fights his dawning realisation that control costs more than it gains.","outcome":"Kael gives up the toll gate and the monopoly claim. The central skybridge ends as a Cartel chokepoint and endures as a public crossing.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_standoff"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What Remains","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_wardens_accord","title":"The Open Charts","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya publishes her charts and the finding about shared crossings. The Wardens, moved by the survivors' accounts, accept her work. Kael attends and agrees to a toll settlement in labour and goods, in keeping with wind-debt, in place of the Cartel's rising fees.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Establish a shared system for maintaining the network.","conflict":"The Wardens distrust Kael, and Veya must accept credit shared with others instead of the recognition she wanted.","outcome":"The Toll War cools into a fragile accord, and Veya's charts become public knowledge.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_choice"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"The Mill Turns Again","summary":"In The Hollow, Maris sees grain shipments cross the central bridge under the new accord. The Grain Levy is eased. Veya visits and thanks her, and Maris acknowledges that hiding for her isle was as brave as standing.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Confirm that The Hollow is fed and that the friendship has survived.","conflict":"Maris's reluctance to forgive and trust tests the friendship, and the bridge's dual nature remains unresolved for the isles.","outcome":"Maris forgives Veya and the friendship is settled. The isles keep drifting, and the bridge stands because people keep crossing it together.","depends_on":["scn_wardens_accord"]},{"id":"scn_emberroost_new_weaving","title":"A New Weaving","summary":"At Emberroost, Wardens and Cartel apprentices braid new cables for the central skybridge side by side. Kael pays his wind-debt with labour at the forge, and Veya records the bridge's colours as it both ends and endures.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Begin repairing the network on shared terms.","conflict":"Old resentments between the factions linger, and the isles are still drifting apart.","outcome":"A new weaving begins. The bridge is accepted as both ending and enduring, and its meaning is held by those who choose to cross.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_harvest"]}]}]}
